 CO4.3c  LOAD SENSITIVITY - p99 response time vs offered load
==============================================================================
      Rate   Offered     FCFS     SSTF     SCAN   C-SCAN     LOOK   C-LOOK
   (req/ms)      load   p99 ms   p99 ms   p99 ms   p99 ms   p99 ms   p99 ms
      0.15      24%       8.1      7.4     15.9     15.0      7.6      8.3
      0.25      40%      10.9      9.6     18.8     17.0      9.8     10.7
      0.35      56%      14.8     12.1     24.0     20.4     12.7     14.6
      0.45      72%      25.3     16.3     28.1     24.7     16.4     18.8
      0.55      88%     122.7     29.9     40.0     32.6     23.1     27.9

   Reading of the sweep: at light load every scheduler meets the 10 ms
   target and the choice barely matters. The algorithms only separate
   once the device saturates -- which is precisely the regime Section D
   specifies. At the 90%+ load design point no single spindle meets a
   10 ms p99 under ANY scheduling policy, so the honest engineering
   conclusion is that scheduling alone is insufficient: the block tier
   must be striped (RAID-10) or moved to NVMe, where the seek term
   vanishes and the scheduler's job reduces to merging and fairness.

